SUMMARY:NEW EVENT - 👻🌙 The Ghosts of Cabbagetown
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 👻🌙 The Ghosts of Cabbageto
 wn\n\n### A 90-Minute Evening Ghost Walk Through One of Toronto’s Most H
 istoric Neighbourhoods\n\nCabbagetown has beautiful Victorian houses\, qui
 et streets\, old cemeteries\, and a history that goes back generations.\nI
 t also has ghosts.\n\nJoin me for a **90-minute evening walking tour throu
 gh Cabbagetown**\, where we'll explore some of the neighbourhood's strange
 st stories\, unsettling legends\, and darker pieces of Toronto's past.\n\n
 We'll begin beneath the glass of **Allan Gardens**\, then make our way thr
 ough the streets of Cabbagetown\, stopping along the way for stories of my
 sterious creatures\, haunted buildings\, old prisons\, cemeteries\, restle
 ss spirits\, and the people who may never have quite left.\nThis isn't a t
 raditional history walk.\n\nIt's a **ghost tour** — so expect some histo
 ry\, some local legends\, a little mystery\, and a few stories that are di
 fficult to explain.\nAnd\, of course\, we'll have a few laughs along the w
 ay.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](htt
 ps://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We
 'll Explore\n\nOur route will take us through some of Cabbagetown's most a
 tmospheric locations\, including:\n🌿 **Allan Gardens** — ghosts benea
 th the glass\n🐾 **Winchester Square Park** — the strange story of Cab
 bagetown's Tunnel Monster\n🍸 **The Winchester Hotel** — spirits that 
 may have never checked out\n🏚️ **Winchester Street** — haunted hous
 es and Victorian secrets\n⛓️ **The Don Jail & Bridgepoint** — where 
 the walls remember everything\n🐄 **Riverdale Farm** — and its strange
  connection to the old Don Jail\n⚰️ **The Toronto Necropolis** — a c
 ity of the dead beneath a city of the living\n🕯️ **St. James Town & S
 t. James' Cemetery** — where the living and the dead share the same neig
 hbourhood\nAnd much\, much more...\n\n***\n\n## 🌙 What Makes This Tour 
 Different?\n\nThis is a **new ghost walk for the group**\, created specifi
 cally around Cabbagetown.\nRather than simply walking from one location to
  another\, the route has been **curated around the stories** so that each 
 stop connects to the next.\n\nWe'll move through the neighbourhood at a co
 mfortable pace\, stopping along the way while I share the stories behind t
 he places we're visiting.\nSome stories are historical.\nSome are local le
 gends.\nSome are downright strange.\nYou'll have to decide for yourself wh
 ich ones you believe. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ A Little About the Tour\n\
 nThis is a **90-minute evening walk**.\nWe will be walking outdoors throug
 hout the tour and will **not be entering buildings**.\nSome locations may 
 be viewed from outside or from nearby public spaces.\nPlease be respectful
  of residents\, private property\, and cemetery grounds as we make our way
  through the neighbourhood.\n\n***\n\n## 📍 Meetup Details\n\n🕚 **Mee
 ting Time:** 6:30 PM\nI will only wait **5 minutes** before we begin.\n
 🫎 **Meeting Location:** Outside the **Palm House at Allan Gardens (this
  BIG WHITE building)**\nLook for me in my **Moose Hat!**\n🏁 **End Point
 :** Parliament Street & Wellesley Street East\n🚶 **Walking Time:** Appr
 oximately 90 minutes\n👻 **Pace:** Comfortable\, steady walking pace\n\n
 ***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathew
 maclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThe $10 fee help
 s support the group and covers the **extra research\, preparation\, and cu
 ration that goes into creating these ghost walks**.\nThese aren't simply w
 alks where we meet up and wander around.\nI've put together a specific rou
 te\, researched the stories\, and created a series of stops designed to tu
 rn the walk into an actual **storytelling experience**.\nYou're paying for
  the experience — not just the walking.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\
 n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧
  Water\n🔦 A little extra light if you have it\n👻 An open mind\nAnd m
 aybe don't wander off by yourself.\nYou never know who's walking behind yo
 u.\n\n***\n\n## ⚠️ A Quick Note\n\nSometimes things happen and I may n
 eed to cancel or change an event.\nPlease keep an eye on the event page fo
 r updates.\nYou can RSVP ahead of time — or **just show up on the day if
  you're not sure about your schedule.**\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?
 \n\nThis walk is for anyone who enjoys:\n👻 Ghost stories and local lege
 nds\n🏙️ Toronto history\n🚶 Social walking\n📸 Exploring differen
 t neighbourhoods\n🕯️ Strange and unusual stories\n😂 A good story w
 ithout taking ourselves too seriously\nYou don't have to be a believer.\nY
 ou don't even have to be scared.\nJust come for the walk and see what you 
 think.\n\n###\n\n**Organizer:** Mathew\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@ho
 tmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n### **👋 Com
 e for the stories.**\n\n### **🚶 Stay for the walk.**\n\n### **👻 And 
 keep an eye out for who might be walking with us.**
